    "title": "SCOTUS Weighs Post-Election Ballot Counting: Attorney Breaks Down What Could Sway the Case",
    "text": "The Supreme Court heard arguments in Bost v. Illinois Board of Elections, a case challenging a state law that allows mail-in ballots to be counted for two weeks after Election Day. Civil rights attorney Bobbie Anne Cox joined NTD’s Tiffany Meier to explain what could give the GOP lawmaker standing before the Court, and how a ruling could ripple through other states.\nSupreme Court Weighs Post-Election Ballot Counting: Attorney Breaks Down What Could Sway the Case\nThe Supreme Court heard arguments in Bost v. Illinois Board of Elections, a case challenging a state law that allows mail-in ballots to be counted for two weeks after Election Day.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 10/8/2025, 11:59:32 PM EDT",
